{sov: Notes}
6/8 Wynton Kelly Pulse: Built around a famous 6/8 (or 3/4) modal jazz-blues
ostinato in G Major/G Mixolydian with a distinct 6th-to-m7th vamp movement.

Harmonic Shift: The IV chord (C7) maintains the G tremolo/vamp feel underneath,
while the turnaround uses sharp altered chromatic steps (D7alt to Eb7alt back
to D7alt).

Modal Improvisation: Soloists typically stick to G Mixolydian over the G7, C
Mixolydian over C7, and altered scale choices over the D7alt / Eb7alt turnaround.

Comping Style: Keep rhythm comping sparse, spacey, and focused on smooth voice
leading rather than heavy strumming.
{eov}